WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.430
- Okay, wait, I don't
wanna not talk about this,

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.616
'cause you've also got a
crime movie with Brad Pitt.

00:00:03.616 --> 00:00:04.449
- Yeah.
(crowd cheers)

00:00:04.449 --> 00:00:06.417
- So, it's out this summer?
- Yeah.

00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:07.650
- So, what's that about?

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.950
- You know, I've always had a dream

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.330
of being in an action movie

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.920
where you get like all the explosions

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.320
and the slow motion walk,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.240
you know what I mean?
- Yeah.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.440
- And I got to do it and I
got to do it with Brad Pitt.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.186
And I was like, "I know you lying."

00:00:21.186 --> 00:00:22.680
(both laugh)

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.370
Yeah and I got to be blonde.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:25.720
I was like, "Yes, I get to be blonde,

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.930
I always wanna try it." (crowd laughs)

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.979
- So, you're still rebelling?
- I'm still rebelling.

00:00:29.979 --> 00:00:30.950
(all laughing)

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.890
That is literally kinda what
my hair looked like in college.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:35.024
And I was like, "Oh, that's
a little too close to home."

00:00:35.024 --> 00:00:35.857
(crowd laughing)

00:00:35.857 --> 00:00:38.260
But yeah, it's a great, great
film called "Bullet Train,"

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.250
directed by David Leitch,

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.650
who did "Atomic Blonde" and "Deadpool".

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.900
And we did this in the
middle of the quarantine,

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.820
so like in October-

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.070
- But you worked all in
quarantine, that's cool.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:51.360
- I am insane, I told you I was a rebel.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.193
- I worked too,

00:00:52.193 --> 00:00:53.674
I never stopped here.
- I know.

00:00:53.674 --> 00:00:54.940
- Yeah.
- I don't know how-

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.390
- It was a nice distraction.
- I feel like I need

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.755
to be interviewing you,
so you can have a break.

00:00:58.755 --> 00:00:59.630
(Kelly laughs)
- Trust me, I'm tired,

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:00.463
I'm gonna have a weekend.
- You wanna switch?

00:01:00.463 --> 00:01:02.310
No don't switch.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.143
- It's kinda nice though,

00:01:03.143 --> 00:01:05.290
because I don't feel like I
was affected during quarantine

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.980
like everybody else was in that sense.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:07.984
- So, yeah, 'cause you were still

00:01:07.984 --> 00:01:08.817
doing something.
- Because I had

00:01:08.817 --> 00:01:10.548
to still keep going, so
there was no time to process.

00:01:10.548 --> 00:01:11.820
- It was the same with "Bullet Train."

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.460
We filmed on Sony, they built a train.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.090
They built cars of the train.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.960
There was a huge screen
with moving pictures going.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.740
I felt like it was very classic Hollywood,

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:21.610
like back in the twenties

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:24.210
when there's 30 people
moving a set and turning this

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.150
and you had to get back

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.360
to the bare minimum.
- That's cool.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.090
- But yeah, it's a huge action movie.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:31.090
The cast is in insane and
I got to fight Brad Pitt.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:31.923
- Yeah.
- Like I get

00:01:31.923 --> 00:01:34.500
to kick Brad Pitt's ass (crowd laughs)

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.790
and it was kinda great

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.260
because this man was the
happiest he had ever been.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.200
And also-
- Oh that's cool.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.590
- We have a lot of fights together

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:43.520
and there's one particular
time that we're fighting

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.960
and I got him in a choke hold
and they would yell, "Cut,"

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.130
and he would just lay my arms.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:48.241
And I was like, "Oh."

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.370
(crowd laughs)

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:50.680
I was like, "How is it possible

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.680
that I feel safer with
you lying in my arms?"

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.530
And it's like, 'cause it's Brad Pitt.

